      "structure_description": "The Y9 hydroxo-carboxylate core has nine metal ions arranged as a tricapped trigonal prism. Eighteen carboxylates from eighteen BTB ligands make it an 18-connected building block with an elongated triangular orthobicupola vertex figure; triangular BTB linkers join these blocks into a three-dimensional (3,18)-connected gea net.",
      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "ph": null,
        "procedure": "Yttrium nitrate hexahydrate, H3BTB and 2-FBA were dissolved in DMF and water in a scintillation vial and heated in a preheated oven. The product was washed repeatedly with DMF, soaked in DMF overnight and solvent-exchanged into MeOH for one week.",
